1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,279
And again before you despair hear this.
再一次，在你感到绝望之前，先听这句话。

2
00:00:03,279 --> 00:00:10,560
Being human means experiencing the full spectrum of emotion joy grief anger loneliness love.
做人就意味着体验情绪的整个光谱：快乐、悲伤、愤怒、孤独与爱。

3
00:00:10,560 --> 00:00:14,159
None of it is good or bad it just is.
她认为，这些感受本身没有好坏，它们就是存在着。

4
00:00:14,159 --> 00:00:19,350
Just like some people turn to cheap dopamine to escape sadness or boredom.
就像有人借她所说的“廉价多巴胺”来逃避悲伤或无聊，

5
00:00:19,360 --> 00:00:26,080
We run from loneliness because we've never learned to live with it to get curious about it to befriend it.
我们也躲开孤独，因为没有学过与它相处、好奇地了解它，甚至与它为友。

6
00:00:26,080 --> 00:00:29,430
So ask yourself when do you feel most alone.
所以问问自己：什么时候最感到孤独？

7
00:00:29,440 --> 00:00:33,520
Is it at night in the mornings on father's day on mother's day.
在夜里、早晨，还是父亲节、母亲节？

8
00:00:33,520 --> 00:00:38,240
Or when you see couples or maybe you see someone being held in a way you long for.
看见情侣时？或者看到有人得到自己渴望的拥抱时？

9
00:00:38,240 --> 00:00:44,080
Are there any other triggers what unhealthy patterns do you usually engage in when it happens.
还有别的触发点吗？这种感受出现时，你通常会采用哪些不健康的模式？

10
00:00:44,080 --> 00:00:46,400
What does that pattern reveal to you.
那个模式又透露出什么？

11
00:00:46,400 --> 00:00:51,839
Because once you have a name for it you can then create a ritual to meet it.
一旦能给它命名，你就可以设计一个小仪式去回应它。

12
00:00:51,839 --> 00:00:56,080
Say it's 6 00 p m on a wednesday and you're aching for someone to hold you.
比如，周三晚上六点，你特别想有人抱抱你。

13
00:00:56,080 --> 00:00:58,400
You don't have that person so what now.
但你没有这样一个人，那接下来怎么办？

14
00:00:58,400 --> 00:01:01,360
How do you create a healthy ritual for coping.
怎样建立一种健康的应对仪式？

15
00:01:01,360 --> 00:01:05,190
How can you hold yourself until the wave passes.
在这一阵情绪过去之前，你怎样给自己一点支持？

16
00:01:05,200 --> 00:01:08,640
Rituals are powerful because they are personal.
她认为，仪式有力量，是因为它们是个人化的。

17
00:01:08,640 --> 00:01:13,680
Maybe you get yourself a giant teddy bear you know or or a weighted blanket.
也许给自己一个大玩具熊，或者一条重力毯，这是她举的个人例子。

18
00:01:13,680 --> 00:01:16,880
Maybe you create a playlist that feels like a hug.
或者建个像拥抱一样的歌单，

19
00:01:16,880 --> 00:01:20,960
One you can cry to dance to chant through or breathe through.
让你可以跟着哭、跳舞、吟唱或呼吸。

20
00:01:20,960 --> 00:01:26,800
The purpose of this is not to get rid of your loneliness but to help you cope with the wave.
目的并非把孤独赶走，而是帮你应对这一波感受。

21
00:01:26,800 --> 00:01:33,599
Maybe you light a candle and send a voice note to someone simply saying hey I'm feeling a little lonely today.
也许点支蜡烛，给人发条语音，只是说：“嘿，我今天有点孤单。”

22
00:01:33,599 --> 00:01:36,800
And just to be clear because I know someone is going to argue about it.
说清楚一点，因为她知道可能有人会对此争论，

23
00:01:36,800 --> 00:01:40,320
You don't reach out to people solely so that they can help you.
她说，不要仅仅为了让别人帮你才主动联系。

24
00:01:40,320 --> 00:01:44,640
No you reach out to help yourself first and foremost.
你主动联系，首先也是为了帮助自己。

25
00:01:44,640 --> 00:01:48,800
Sometimes connection isn't about someone swooping in and saving the day.
有时，联结并不是有人突然出现、拯救一切。

26
00:01:48,800 --> 00:01:54,159
It's about the principle of treating yourself like someone worth hearing out.
而是把自己当作一个值得被耐心听完的人。

27
00:01:54,159 --> 00:01:58,320
Maybe they won't respond maybe maybe they won't do anything at all.
也许对方不会回应，也许什么都不会做。

28
00:01:58,320 --> 00:02:02,320
But now your loneliness doesn't just live inside your chest.
但现在，你的孤独不再只是闷在胸口里面。

29
00:02:02,320 --> 00:02:09,920
It exists out there in the world too it's been spoken witnessed shared yeah.
它也存在于外部世界：被说出来、被见证、被分享。

30
00:02:09,920 --> 00:02:14,880
And you'd be surprised what can happen when you stop bottling everything up.
当你不再把所有事都闷在心里时，也许会惊讶于随后发生的事。

31
00:02:14,880 --> 00:02:20,719
Yes the world can be cold and cruel but it's also warm it's both.
是的，世界可能冷漠、残酷，但它也有温暖的一面，两者并存。

32
00:02:20,719 --> 00:02:25,360
And you have to believe in that warmth enough to keep reaching out for it okay.
作者说，要对那份温暖保留足够信心，才会继续主动伸手联系。

33
00:02:25,360 --> 00:02:34,960
And if the people in your life truly don't care about you then ditch them dump them like a hot potato okay and go find people who do.
如果身边人真的不在乎你，作者激烈地说，放下他们，去找在乎你的人。

34
00:02:34,960 --> 00:02:40,320
You are not helpless help yourself first and watch help start coming into your life.
她说，你并非无能为力，先帮助自己，也许会看到帮助进入生活；不作结果保证。

35
00:02:40,320 --> 00:02:43,920
A lot of us walk through the world armored up.
我们很多人像穿着盔甲一样生活。

36
00:02:43,920 --> 00:02:48,719
We tell ourselves stories about how cold or closed off others are.
总给自己讲故事，说别人多么冷漠、多么封闭，

37
00:02:48,719 --> 00:02:53,120
But we don't realize we are the ones not giving people a chance.
却可能没发现，是自己没有给别人了解自己的机会。

38
00:02:53,120 --> 00:02:55,760
Try saying what you need out loud.
试着把需要说出声。

39
00:02:55,760 --> 00:02:59,520
Try letting yourself be seen try talking to strangers.
试着让自己被看见，试着跟陌生人聊聊。

40
00:02:59,520 --> 00:03:04,080
Yes literally even as an experiment just try it for a week.
她说，真的，可以把它当一次实验，先试一周。

41
00:03:04,080 --> 00:03:08,230
Ask someone for help give a compliment say good morning.
向人求助、夸赞一句、道声早安。

42
00:03:08,240 --> 00:03:14,719
These little moments remind us that connection is always available even in the smallest doses.
这些小瞬间提醒她，即使以很小的份量，联结也可能存在。

43
00:03:14,719 --> 00:03:17,670
It can be a simple moment like me two days ago in the park.
可以是这样的小事：她说，前两天自己在公园时，

44
00:03:17,680 --> 00:03:22,719
The other day I saw a guy climbing the stairs to to a place I wanted to be.
看到一个人正走上台阶，通往她想去的地方。

45
00:03:22,719 --> 00:03:23,839
I was curious about the space.
我对那个地方很好奇。

46
00:03:23,839 --> 00:03:28,080
And I said hia excuse me could you please go up there and check how busy it is there.
于是我说：你好，打扰一下，你能上去看看那里有多忙吗？

47
00:03:28,080 --> 00:03:31,839
And let me know so I don't have to walk all the way there please thank you.
然后告诉我，这样我就不必自己走那么远。麻烦了，谢谢。

48
00:03:31,839 --> 00:03:36,560
And he said oh sure he went there found out came back and told me that was it.
他说，当然。就走过去看了看，回来告诉我，仅此而已。

49
00:03:36,560 --> 00:03:40,000
I didn't ask him expecting him to say yes I just asked him because you know.
我并不是预期他一定答应才开口，我只是问了一下。

50
00:03:40,000 --> 00:03:44,960
If he ignored me fine I wouldn't have assumed anything about him I won't think he's a terrible person.
如果他没理我，我也不会因此推断他的性格，不会觉得他是个糟糕的人。

51
00:03:44,960 --> 00:03:49,200
I would have just done it myself or asked someone else and I won't also think I'm terrible either.
我会自己去，或问另一个人；也不会觉得自己很糟糕。

52
00:03:49,200 --> 00:03:57,200
I don't talk to strangers to prove that people are good or bad I talk to strangers because humans are supposed to talk to each other simple.
我与陌生人说话，不是为了证明人好或坏；她认为，人本来就可以彼此交谈，就这么简单。
